Why isn't p[g] logit-transformed instead of log? It's clearly used in the dbinom() in the Abundance model. I must be missing something. Thanks in advance.
# Define the likelihood for (g in 1:nsites){
# Detection probability model log(p[g]) <- -(1/(2*sigma*sigma))*dist[g]*dist[g]

# Observation model
for(k in 1:2){
y[g,k] ~ dbinom(p[g], N[g])
}

# Abundance model including GAM
N[g] ~ dpois(lam[g])
lam[g] <- exp(beta0 + smooth[g] )
smooth[g] <- inprod(Z.mat[g,], b[])
}

